<title>JAPAN: Bridgestone selling Korean batteries in Japan.</title>
<headline>Bridgestone selling Korean batteries in Japan.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bridgestone Corp said on Thursday that it recently began selling car batteries in Japan made by a South Korean joint venture between the Daewoo Group and General Motors Corp's Delco unit.</p>
<p>The company initially imported 5,000 units for sale at the 175 retail tyre outlets operated in Japan by its subsidiary Bridgestone FVS Co, a spokesman said.</p>
<p>The retail prices of the batteries, sold under a Bridgestone brand name, are 15 to 30 percent below Japanese and foreign car batteries currently sold at the shops.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodity Desk, 81-3-3432-6179</p>
